From 9bd30acc9d76bf14092b955d435254ccdc9f06fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:03:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Changed: Show the app as DevShell with its own welcome
 message and links

The app name is DevShell, a fork of Termux. The local shell welcomes
with ~/.termux/motd.sh, which the login script prefers over the
package's motd, written in the language of the app with the manual,
releases and issues of this repository, and where to report package
issues to Termux. A motd.sh without the app's marker line is left
alone. Help opens the manual of this repository instead of the Termux
wiki, the about and issue reports start with this app's links, and the
donation link of Termux is not shown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
